00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:12,250
Lateral surface area, total surface area of rectangular prism and cube.

2
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:21,600
Lateral surface area, total surface area of rectangular prism.

3
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:27,500
Lateral surface area

4
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:42,150
Lateral surface area of rectangular prism is sum of area of four side faces of rectangular prism.

5
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:51,270
Example: given rectangular prism with length 8 cm,

6
00:00:51,270 --> 00:01:01,350
Example: given rectangular prism with length 8 cm, width 5 cm and height 4 cm.

7
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:10,520
Calculate lateral surface area of that rectangular prism.

8
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:20,650
To calculate lateral surface area of rectangular prism we do as follows:

9
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:30,850
Lateral surface area of rectangular prism equals area of rectangular prism when unfolded has:

10
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:46,520
Length is: 5 + 8 + 5 + 8 = 26 (cm)

11
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:54,450
That is equal to perimeter of base face of prism.

12
00:01:55,150 --> 00:02:05,270
Width 4 cm (that is equal to prism height).

13
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:13,500
Therefore, lateral surface area of that rectangular prism is:

14
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:26,620
26 x 4 = 104 (cm<sup>2</sup>)

15
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:54,270
Conclusion: To calculate lateral surface area of rectangular prism we take base perimeter times height (same unit).

16
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:10,770
Total surface area

17
00:03:12,070 --> 00:03:27,970
Total surface area of rectangular prism is sum of lateral surface area and area of two bases.

18
00:03:29,970 --> 00:03:47,370
Example: given rectangular prism with length 8 cm, width 5 cm and height 4 cm.

19
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:58,670
Calculate total surface area of that rectangular prism.

20
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:07,650
To calculate total surface area of rectangular prism we do as follows:

21
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:14,700
Calculate area of one base face.

22
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:25,250
Take lateral surface area plus area of two base faces.

23
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:37,900
Rectangular prism in example above has area of one base face is:

24
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:47,870
8 x 5 = 40 (cm<sup>2</sup>)

25
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:56,350
Therefore, total surface area of that rectangular prism is:

26
00:04:56,350 --> 00:05:11,820
104 + 40 x 2 = 184 (cm<sup>2</sup>)

